<div style="border: 2px solid #1a5276; padding: 15px; text-align: center; background-color: #e0f2f7; margin-bottom: 20px;">
    <h1 style="color: #1a5276; margin: 0; font-size: 2em;">Lesson Planner – Theme # In Ten Years, I Will... – Lesson # 4</h1>
    <p style="color: #1a5276; margin: 5px 0 0 0; font-size: 1.2em;">Complete this planner five times per theme, once per lesson (Lesson 1 through Lesson 5).</p>
</div>

<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Lesson #:</b> 4</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Skills Focus:</b> Writing</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Grade:</b> 10th Grade (CEFR: B1.1)</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Scenario:</b> Future Plans and Time Capsule</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Theme:</b> In Ten Years, I Will...</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Date(s):</b> From ___ to ___</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="2"><b>Learning Sequence Time:</b> 45–50 min</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="3">
            <b>Specific Objective:</b>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Writing: Productive: Write simple, informal emails/letters. Interactive: Participate in a written discussion on paper, through apps, online, or in a forum discussion.</p>
            <b>Learning Outcome:</b>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Writing: Can write a letter to their future self, describing detailed career goals and the steps needed to achieve them (e.g., "In five years, I will be pursuing a degree in marine biology at the University of Panama, supported by an internship at a conservation organization.").<br>Can participate in a written discussion about time capsule items (e.g., "The teacher said that we should include photos of our class in the project.").<br>Can write a brief note explaining a personal item for the time capsule (e.g., "I have chosen this book because it will help me grow.").</p>
        </td>
    </tr>
</table>

<h2 style="color: #1a5276; text-align: center;">The Six Action-Oriented Approach (AOA) Lesson Stages</h2>
<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <thead style="background-color: #f0f8ff;">
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 30%;">Stage & Description</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 55%;">Activities & Teacher Actions</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 15%;">Estimated Date and Time</th>
        </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin: 0 0 5px 0;">STAGE 1 — Warm-up / Pre-task</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Engagement, Modeling and Clarification</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Warm-up:</b> The teacher begins by projecting images of various career paths (e.g., software developer, engineer, marine biologist, doctor) and famous individuals who achieved their goals. Students are asked to quickly jot down 2-3 words that come to mind for each image in their notebooks. The teacher then writes "In Ten Years, I Will..." on the board and invites students to complete the sentence orally with one idea. This activates prior knowledge and vocabulary related to future plans.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Modeling:</b> The teacher models writing a short paragraph about their own (or a fictional) future career goal, using modals for possibilities and future continuous. For example, "In ten years, I might be developing educational software. I will be working with a team to enhance learning experiences for students." The teacher explicitly highlights the grammatical structures (e.g., "might pursue," "will be working") and target vocabulary (e.g., 'software developer,' 'enhance,' 'career'). The teacher also focuses on the pronunciation of /iː/ in words like 'achieve' and stress in 'problem-solving' while speaking the example.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Clarification (CCQs):</b>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"If I say 'I might pursue a career in medicine,' does it mean I am 100% sure, or is it a possibility?" (Expected answer: A possibility, not 100% sure.)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"When I say 'I will be working as a data analyst,' am I talking about a finished action, or an ongoing plan in the future?" (Expected answer: An ongoing plan in the future.)</li>
                </ul>
                </p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">10 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin: 0 0 5px 0;">STAGE 2 — Presentation</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Input of new language/content connected to Scenario: "Future Plans and Time Capsule"</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Material:</b> The teacher distributes a short, informal example letter written by a high school student to their future self, detailing career goals and a personal item for a time capsule. The letter includes examples of modals for career possibilities, future continuous for ongoing plans, and reported speech (e.g., "My teacher said that I should consider an internship.").</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Competence:</b> Students will understand the structure and linguistic features of an informal letter/note expressing future plans and explaining personal item choices, specifically targeting the ability to write productively and interactively in written form.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Comprehension tasks:</b> Students read the example letter individually.
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Gist Question:</b> "What is the main purpose of this letter?" (Expected answer: To describe the writer's future goals and a time capsule item.)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>True/False:</b> Students answer T/F questions based on the text (e.g., "The writer is absolutely certain about becoming a data analyst. T/F").</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Information Matching:</b> Students match phrases from the letter to their grammatical function (e.g., "I might pursue..." with 'possibility').</li>
                </ul>
                </p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">10 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin: 0 0 5px 0;">STAGE 3 — Preparation / Practice</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Accuracy focus on Writing</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Skill & Content:</b> Students will practice writing sentences and short paragraphs using modals for career possibilities (might, could, will), future continuous for ongoing plans (will be working, will be studying), and reported speech (said that I should/could/might). Vocabulary includes 'career,' 'future,' 'goals,' 'possibilities,' 'internship,' 'skills,' 'leadership,' 'problem-solving,' 'critical thinking,' 'pursue,' 'develop,' 'achieve,' 'succeed,' 'enhance,' 'relevant.'</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Detailed Procedure:</b>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>1. Controlled Practice (Sentence Completion):</b> The teacher provides a worksheet with sentence starters related to future plans and time capsule items. Students complete the sentences using target grammar and vocabulary.
                        <ul>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 2px; text-align: justify;">"In five years, I _________________ (pursue/might) a degree in _________________ (education/technology)."</li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 2px; text-align: justify;">"By 2030, I _________________ (work/will be) as a _________________ (software developer/data analyst)."</li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 2px; text-align: justify;">"My parents _________________ (said/told) that I _________________ (should/could) gain more _________________ (experience/training)."</li>
                        </ul>
                    </li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>2. Semi-controlled Practice (Paragraph Building):</b> Students are given a list of key words (e.g., 'career,' 'goals,' 'develop,' 'skills,' 'internship,' 'will,' 'might,' 'should'). They must write a short paragraph (3-4 sentences) about a specific career goal, incorporating at least three words from the list, one modal, and one future continuous structure. The teacher circulates, offering immediate written feedback on grammar and vocabulary usage.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>3. Pair Interaction/Peer Check (Note for Time Capsule):</b> In pairs, students write a brief note (2-3 sentences) explaining a personal item they would put in a time capsule. They then exchange notes with their partner and use a simple checklist (e.g., "Did my partner use 'will' or 'might'? Did they explain *why* the item is important?") to give written feedback on clarity, grammar, and vocabulary. The teacher guides them on how to write constructive feedback. (e.g., "You used 'will be working' correctly, but you might want to add more detail about your 'skills'.")</li>
                </ul>
                </p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">15 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin: 0 0 5px 0;">STAGE 4 — Performance / Production</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Communicative task where students USE the language in a realistic scenario: "Future Plans and Time Capsule"</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Task Format:</b> Students will write a personal letter to their future self, addressing it "Dear Future Self," and detailing their career goals and the steps they plan to take to achieve them over the next five to ten years. They will also include a short paragraph explaining one item they would place in a time capsule that represents their current aspirations or a significant memory, similar to the example note practice in Stage 3.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Procedure:</b>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Students are given a "Letter to My Future Self" template (a blank paper with a simple heading).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">They must include at least three specific career goals, using modals of possibility (e.g., "I might pursue...") and future continuous (e.g., "I will be studying..., I will be working as...").</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">They should incorporate advice they have received, using reported speech (e.g., "My teacher said that I should develop my problem-solving skills").</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">They must also describe one personal item for the time capsule, explaining its significance and connection to their goals, using vocabulary such as 'relevant,' 'represents,' 'achieve,' 'grow.' (e.g., "I am including this book on leadership because it will help me develop critical thinking skills needed for my future career.").</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">The teacher encourages the use of a wide range of target vocabulary (e.g., 'education,' 'training,' 'internship,' 'experience,' 'skills,' 'community service,' 'opportunities') and prompts students to write detailed sentences rather than just simple statements.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Students are reminded to review their work for grammatical accuracy and clear expression before completion.</li>
                </ul>
                </p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">10 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin: 0 0 5px 0;">STAGE 5 — Assessment / Post-task</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Formative assessment strategy</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Assessment Task:</b> Students will submit their "Letter to My Future Self" for formative assessment. The letters will eventually be placed into a physical or digital class time capsule to be opened at a later date (e.g., at graduation).</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Evaluation Criteria (Teacher Checklist/Rubric for Writing):</b>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Use of Target Grammar:</b> Appropriate and accurate use of modals for possibilities (might, could, will), future continuous, and reported speech (e.g., "My teacher said that I should..."). (2 points)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Vocabulary:</b> Effective incorporation of at least 5-7 target vocabulary words related to career goals, skills, and opportunities (e.g., 'internship,' 'leadership,' 'problem-solving,' 'achieve,' 'relevant'). (2 points)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Content & Clarity:</b> Clear description of career goals and the steps needed to achieve them; well-explained reason for time capsule item. (2 points)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Organization:</b> Letter follows a logical structure (introduction, body paragraphs for goals, conclusion/time capsule item). (1 point)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Sentence Structure & Spelling:</b> Sentences are varied and grammatically sound; minimal spelling errors. (1 point)</li>
                </ul>
                </p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student Self-Assessment / Exit Ticket:</b> Students complete a short reflection on a sticky note:
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"One new vocabulary word I used successfully in my letter was ___________."</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"I found it easiest/most challenging to write about _______________ because _______________."</li>
                </ul>
                </p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">5 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin: 0 0 5px 0;">STAGE 6 — Reflection</h3>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student Self-Reflection:</b>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What part of writing your letter to your future self did you enjoy the most, and why?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What is one specific skill or grammatical structure you feel more confident using in your writing after today's lesson?"</li>
                </ul>
                </p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Teacher Reflection:</b>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"The practice activities (Stage 3) were effective because students demonstrated understanding of modals and future continuous in their written work. The peer-check for the time capsule note also promoted active learning and self-correction, enhancing their writing accuracy."</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"For future lessons, I might provide more sentence frames for the reported speech part to ensure all students confidently incorporate advice into their writing, as some struggled with its structure. I also need to ensure more varied adjectives are used."</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"The pronunciation focus on /i:/ in 'achieve' and 'believe' seemed to resonate, and I will continue to integrate pronunciation checks during oral interaction."</li>
                </ul>
                </p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Connection to Next Lesson:</b> This writing task prepares students for Lesson 5, where they will engage in a Mediation & Integration activity, focusing on creating the actual time capsule. They will summarize their future plans and item explanations for a presentation or a class "time capsule ceremony," requiring them to verbally mediate their written thoughts and integrate 21st Century Skills.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">5 min</td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>